  - [38;5;153mset[39m returns [38;5;153mfalse[39m when the backend throws on write, instead of propagating
  - A backend that throws on access yields a working in-memory store
  - [38;5;153m"password"[39m is not a registered key, so [38;5;153mset("password", …)[39m throws — the security constraint from section 2 as an
    executable assertion rather than a comment

  What this deliberately does not cover: the DOM wiring in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m — theme class application, field pre-fill, the
  checkbox branch. Testing that needs jsdom or Playwright, both of which you ruled out. That code stays thin and
  verified by hand precisely because it's untested; all the branching logic sits in [38;5;153mprefs.js[39m where the tests are. Worth
  knowing that's the gap rather than discovering it later.

  Does the testing approach look right? If so, I'll write the spec to
  [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/specs/2026-09-16-user-preferences-storage-design.md[39m (uncommitted) for your review.

